readMaple -- Read the result of a previous Maple computation.
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        readMaple(fn)
  * Inputs:
      * fn, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, 

Description
===========

Read the result of a previous Maple computation stored in the file fn via the
option *note store: store, of *note callMaple: callMaple,.

*note callMaple: callMaple,( ... , *note store: store,=>fn); readMaple(fn)

will return the same result as

callMaple( ... )

Ways to use readMaple:
======================

  * "readMaple(String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note readMaple: readMaple, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in MapleInterface.m2:309:0.

File: MapleInterface.info, Node: store, Prev: readMaple, Up: Top

store -- Store result of a Maple computation in a file.
*******************************************************

Description
===========

If the option store=>fn with a *note String: (Macaulay2Doc)String, fn is given
then *note callMaple: callMaple,  stores the result of the Maple computation in
a file named fn.

This data can be read by the command *note readMaple: readMaple,.

Functions with optional argument named store:
=============================================

  * "callMaple(...,store=>...)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note store: store, is a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

